{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>And you shall know today.</b> If so, it is undoubtedly fitting that you contemplate and know all parts of the contradictoriness." "<b>And you shall restore to your heart.</b> After contemplation, you shall restore to your heart the true part among them — namely, <b>that HaShem is the Elohim</b>, the eternal Governor made known <b>in the heavens above and on the earth beneath</b>. For indeed their order and interconnectedness and the end discerned from them point to this, which cannot be grasped from anything else; and through them it becomes known that there exists a directing Being who brought all this into being for a directed end from Him." "<b>There is none else.</b> And from this you know that there is none else — for it is of necessity that all this cannot exist through the power of any being separate from matter to a high degree, exalted to the utmost of possibility; and it is impossible for there to be more than one at this level of exaltedness than which there is none like it, since among separate beings number cannot apply unless they are unequal in degree."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:34.188652156Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}